"""This project's guard extension: the project's own rules on top of the base guard.

The base guard (``plugin/hub-workflow/hooks/guard.py``) calls ``check(event, cfg)`` for each
tool call it does not deny itself. It runs this file in a child ``python3`` with a timeout:

- ``event`` is the PreToolUse hook input, a dict with ``tool_name`` and ``tool_input``;
- ``cfg`` is this hub's ``hub.json`` as the hooks' reader loads it: a ``HubFile`` object read by
  attribute (``cfg.guard.deny_paths``), not a dict.

``check`` returns ``None`` to keep the base verdict, ``("deny", reason)`` to block the call or
``("ask", reason)`` to ask the user first. An extension only tightens: it never allows what the
base guard denies or asks. Any failure (an exception, another return value, output printed to
stdout, the timeout) makes the guard ask, naming the cause. Use the standard library only: the
hooks run on the system ``python3`` (3.9 or newer).

This file is seeded: ``hub init`` or ``hub sync`` writes it once and never rewrites it.
"""


def check(event, cfg):
    """Keep the base verdict: this project has no guard rule yet."""
    return None
